Many thanks to :

Rodrigo Poblete and
Jan Mark Holzer

It looks like the manual on the Internet is wrong, so if 
you want a service to start even when only one plex is 
available, you must set this variable to ON, as the 
script /var/ase/sbin/lsm_lv_action uses it.

My scenario has two cluster members sharing two disk 
cabinets (15 disks each cabinet). Using LSM, one 
cabinet is the mirror of the other one. Due to an 
electrical failure, one server and one entire cabinet 
crashed. ASE detected this event on the surviving 
server, and tried to relocate the service, but it never 
happened because ASE_PARTIAL_MIRRORING was 
in default (OFF). I don't know why setting it to ON can 
compromise data integrity, as LSM is supposed to take 
care of that.

Thanks and regards
fargo

