Hello,

We have a very similar situation to yours: we use a DEC3000/600 running
DU4.0d.  We use (almost) exclusively mkhybrid (mkisofs-lookalike) and
cdwrite.  The writer is a YAMAHA CRW4260 (which is 6 speed reading, 4 speed
writing and 2 speed rewriting).  We actually have another of these on a
Linux machine.  Both have been in use very intensively for about a year.  I
would recommend them (or even Yamaha in general).  They are not really
cheap though.

Greetings,

Bert.

