From tru64-unix-managers  Tue Dec 15 20:31:39 1998
From: Jon Wright <jon.wright () ui ! com>
Date: Tue, 15 Dec 1998 20:31:39 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY: Running DECwindows/Motif interface; want CDE instead
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96078731111993


Abstract of original problem:

> I was just shipped a DU 4.0B workstation from a customer. When I plugged
it
> in and booted it, it came up with a DECwindows/Motif interface, not the
CDE
> interface.
>
> How do I configure this system to run in CDE mode?

The solution turns out to be trivial. You can set XLOGIN to cde in
/etc/rc.config or you can run /usr/sbin/xsetup and answer the questions
(xsetup just appears to automate the editing process for you). If you want
to switch back, set XLOGIN to xdm (or run xsetup again).

