Dear managers,

Thanks to all who respond and especially to Ray Bellis
alf@northpower.com.au and Jan Koktan who gave me the solution.

DU4.0B doesn't support netmasks which are 'shorter' than the natural
netmask for a particular network address (supernetting) e.g.
255.255.255.0 for a class C address. On the contrary DU4.0D should allow
that ('CIDR' : Classless Inter-Domain Routing).

