Greetings,

   Thanks to Glenn Newbery, Alan Davis, rich <raf@ezunx.com>, and Donn 
Aiken.

   My original question was:
 
   Is it possible to implement shadow passwords on a DU 4.0 system without 
installing Digital's Enhanced Security package?  We'd like to get shadow 
passwords implemented quickly and we don't want to rush into Enhanced 
Security without the proper planning up front.

   Summary of the answers:

   Basically, the answer is that one can't implement shadow passwords on a 
Digital Unix system (without using third-party software) unless you 
install and enable DEC's Enhanced Security package.  Due to the nature of 
the AlphaServer in question, we will be doing a carefully planned 
implementation of Enhanced Security in the not too distant future.

   Thanks again for the prompt responses.  This is quite a valuable 
mailing list.

   More later,
           Ken S. -- <kschu@fnal.gov>

