From tru64-unix-managers  Thu Dec 31 14:38:22 1998
From: Pat Wilson <paw () northstar ! dartmouth ! edu>
Date: Thu, 31 Dec 1998 14:38:22 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: Why so old a sendmail in 4.0D?
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96078731112211

I wrote:
	I've just patched 4.0D with the latest patchkit (#3), and notice
	that sendmail is _still_ reporting "5.65v4.0".  Why aren't
	we at at least 8.8.5 by now?  This is a real problem for me,
	since while I usually just roll my own, _this_ machine is for
	a tur(n)key app, and the vendor pitches a fit if we do any customizations
	(not that it _affects_ anything, mind you - they're just silly).

	I have a feeling that this vendor isn't yet supporting 4.0E yet,
	either. :-<

	So - am I just SOL?

Thanks to all who responded, but especially Richard Jackson , 
who set me on the right path.  It turns out that (a) there _is_ a 
patch for 4.0D that brings sendmail up to 8.8.7 available for contract 
customers, but (b) it's only "unofficially supported". :-<

Support says "The only offical release of sendmail v8 will be in
Digital UNIX 4.0e."

So - either upgrade, or ask *very* nicely for a patchkit
containing IAFWSMTP340.  In general, you're probably better off
upgrading.

Happy New Year!

Pat Wilson
paw@dartmouth.edu

